WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.900
A stream, and nobody consuming it.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.100
The frontend was still polling.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.200
Then: four minutes of nothing.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.500
Progress was saved once per page.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.600
So save it per window instead.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.000
One fact puts a section on screen.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.900
And then the section froze.

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.500
One item, while eight more were read.

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.800
Send it again each time it grows.

10
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.100
Neither was visible to the tests.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.600
The failure message was a dead end.

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.600
They could fix it. We said they could not.

13
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.700
So: situations, not log lines.

14
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.200
The migration had said so all along.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.000
And the report arrives while you watch.

16
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.300
Use the thing. It tells you what is wrong.
